# Day 6: End-to-End Medallion Capstone

## Overview

This project uses PySpark and Delta Lake to build a Bronze, Silver, and Gold data pipeline in Microsoft Fabric. It processes customers, products, orders, and order items from initial and incremental CSV batches.

## Pipeline Stages

- **Bronze:** Reads the four CSV files using explicit schemas and adds `ingested_at`, `source_file`, and `batch_id`.
- **Silver:** Cleans and validates data, removes duplicate business keys, checks relationships between tables, saves rejected records, and uses Delta MERGE to update or insert records.
- **Gold:** Creates `gold_sales_detail` and `gold_monthly_category`, calculates sales and profit, and excludes cancelled orders.

## Run Order

1. Attach the Lakehouse containing the input files.
2. Run the notebook cells in order to define the pipeline functions.
3. Run the final cell to execute the initial batch, incremental batch, and repeated incremental batch.
4. Review the Gold totals and reconciliation report.

## Assumptions

- Customer, product, order, and order item IDs are the business keys.
- Invalid records are rejected and saved with a rejection reason.
- Orders must reference valid customers, and order items must reference valid orders and products.
- Cancelled orders are excluded from Gold sales calculations.
- Reprocessing the same incremental batch should not change the final Gold results.

## Reconciliation and Expected Results

| Metric | Expected |
|---|---:|
| Silver customers | 20 |
| Silver products | 15 |
| Silver orders | 60 |
| Silver order items | 120 |
| Gold sales detail rows | 96 |
| Gold net sales | 220,619.25 |
| Gold profit | 62,469.25 |

The reconciliation report checks duplicate keys, missing required values, invalid relationships, row counts, and financial totals. It is saved under `Files/work/day6/evidence/reconciliation/`.

The repeated incremental run should leave the Gold keys, row count, and financial totals unchanged.

## Performance Decision

I used explicit schemas instead of inferring data types from CSV files. I also selected only the required columns before joining tables, reducing the amount of data processed during joins.

## Conclusion

This project demonstrates incremental data processing, data quality checks, Delta MERGE operations, Gold analytics, and reconciliation across a medallion architecture.